\lispPackageChapter{candlesticks/migrations}

Schema changes live as numbered \texttt{.up.sql} / \texttt{.down.sql}
pairs under \texttt{migrations/} and are applied with
\texttt{cl-migratum}~\cite{cl-migratum}.  The Postmodern driver takes
ownership of Postmodern's top-level connection, so every public function
here opens that connection, does its work, and disconnects.

An optional schema name sets the connection's \texttt{search\_path} first,
which is how the live tests keep their tables out of \texttt{public}.

\section{Functions}

\lispFunctionSubsection{migrations-path}

The directory holding the Candlesticks migration files.

\lispFunctionSubsection{connection-spec->migratum-spec}

Convert a Postmodern connection spec (a list that
\texttt{postmodern:connect} can be applied to) into the keyword spec the
\texttt{cl-migratum} Postmodern driver expects.

\lispSyntax

\lispCall{\texttt{(connection-spec->migratum-spec \lispVar{spec-list})}}

\lispExamples

\begin{lstlisting}
(connection-spec->migratum-spec
 '("db" "u" "pw" "localhost" :port 5432))
; => (:database "db" :user-name "u" :password "pw"
;     :host "localhost" :port 5432)
\end{lstlisting}

\lispFunctionSubsection{run-migrations}

Apply all pending Candlesticks migrations to the database described by
\lispVar{spec-list}.  When \lispVar{schema} is given, it is first set as
the connection's \texttt{search\_path}.

\lispSyntax

\lispCall{\texttt{(run-migrations \lispVar{spec-list} \&optional \lispVar{schema})}}

\lispFunctionSubsection{revert-last-migration}

Revert the most recently applied Candlesticks migration.

\lispFunctionSubsection{pending-migrations}

The Candlesticks migrations that have not yet been applied.

\lispFunctionSubsection{applied-migrations}

The Candlesticks migrations that have already been applied.

\lispFunctionSubsection{latest-migration-id}

The id of the most recently applied Candlesticks migration, or
\texttt{nil}.

\lispFunctionSubsection{migration-status?}

True if at least one Candlesticks migration has been applied to the given
database (in \lispVar{schema}, when given).

\section{Macros}

\lispMacroSubsection{with-migration-driver}

Create a \texttt{cl-migratum} driver for \lispVar{spec-list}, optionally
set the connection's \texttt{search\_path} to \lispVar{schema},
initialize the driver, run \lispVar{body} with it bound to
\lispVar{driver-var}, and disconnect the top-level connection when
\lispVar{body} finishes.

\lispSyntax

\lispCall{\texttt{(with-migration-driver (\lispVar{driver-var} \&optional \lispVar{spec-list} \lispVar{schema}) \&body \lispVar{body})}}
